5,"untouched"],[15.938,0.138,"by"],[16.087,1.025,"circumstance"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"A True Yogi Sees All Beings With Equanimity","visual":["Friend and enemy, saint and sinner","A clod, a stone and gold","The yogi sees them with an equal eye"],"L":["L5"],"say":"Lesson five. A true yogi sees all beings with equanimity. Friends and enemies, relatives and strangers, saints and sinners: the yogi treats them all impartially. To such a person, a clod of earth, a stone and a piece of gold are the same.","start":274.776,"at":275.352,"end":292.728,"words":[[0.1,0.463,"Lesson"],[0.575,0.575,"five"],[1.525,0.1,"A"],[1.637,0.287,"true"],[1.938,0.5,"yogi"],[2.45,0.412,"sees"],[2.875,0.237,"all"],[3.125,0.412,"beings"],[3.55,0.15,"with"],[3.712,0.787,"equanimity"],[4.888,0.425,"Friends"],[5.325,0.1,"and"],[5.438,0.537,"enemies"],[6.175,0.625,"relatives"],[6.888,0.138,"and"],[7.037,0.662,"strangers"],[7.925,0.388,"saints"],[8.325,0.113,"and"],[8.45,0.487,"sinners"],[9.262,0.087,"the"],[9.363,0.4,"yogi"],[9.775,0.338,"treats"],[10.125,0.15,"them"],[10.287,0.2,"all"],[10.5,0.688,"impartially"],[11.55,0.15,"To"],[11.713,0.263,"such"],[11.988,0.075,"a"],[12.075,0.562,"person"],[12.825,0.037,"a"],[12.875,0.25,"clod"],[13.137,0.125,"of"],[13.275,0.375,"earth"],[13.875,0.037,"a"],[13.925,0.525,"stone"],[14.55,0.113,"and"],[14.675,0.062,"a"],[14.75,0.237,"piece"],[15.0,0.125,"of"],[15.137,0.338,"gold"],[15.488,0.062,"are"],[15.562,0.113,"the"],[15.688,0.45,"same"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Meditation Requires Solitude, Control, and Proper Technique","visual":["A clean, quiet place and a firm seat","Spine, neck and head erect, gaze steady","Mind and senses restrained"],"L":["L6"],"say":"Lesson six. Meditation requires solitude, control and proper technique. A clean and quiet space, an erect posture with the spine, neck and head aligned, a steady gaze, and the mind and senses gently restrained. The body's stillness supports the mind's.","start":292.728,"at":293.304,"end"